[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_pks7m")
dialogue_id = "mq_4_30_begin"
record_title = "Era 四: The Ancient Tongue"
text = "PAGE: explorer(MUSEUM_SECONDARY), historian(MUSEUM_PRIMARY)
historian: Good to see you back!
historian: I was starting to feel lonely with the Scribe gone.
historian: What could possess the old man to leave in such a hurry?
historian: He's barely left his studio in decades!
explorer: Oh, you're never too old to go out and explore!
historian: Well, I rather like it here myself.
historian: Besides, he left behind half of his sacred archive in my care, which has been fascinating.
explorer: You can actually read that old stuff?
historian: Well, no, not yet.
historian: But I'm close.
historian: They are almost the same glyphs we use today.
historian: But the meaning has drifted, and there's no grammar at all.
explorer: Even the Scribe said they were sacred chants whose meaning is too divine for us mortals.
historian: They were written down by people, and we're people too, so we must be able to understand them eventually.
explorer: Sounds like you've got your work cut out for you.
explorer: I'll look forward to hearing about what you find!
historian: You really can't sit still, can you?
historian: Fine, I won't bore you with the details.
historian: But I need a favor.
historian: Next time you join a settling expedition, bring a scholar from among the refugees with you.
historian: I'll have them set up a school to tackle this translation project."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
